1. Ordered List (<ol>)
Displays items with numbers.

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Ordered List</title>
</head>
<body>

<h2>Programming Languages</h2>

<ol>
    <li>Python</li>
    <li>Java</li>
    <li>HTML</li>
    <li>CSS</li>
</ol>

</body>
</html>


2. Unordered List (<ul>)

Displays items with bullets.

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Unordered List</title>
</head>
<body>

<h2>Subjects</h2>

<ul>
    <li>DBMS</li>
    <li>Python</li>
    <li>Java</li>
    <li>Web Development</li>
</ul>

</body>
</html>


A table is used to display data in rows and columns.

Basic Table
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Student Table</title>
    <style>
        table{
            border-collapse: collapse;
            width: 50%;
        }

        table, th, td{
            border: 1px solid black;
        }

        th, td{
            padding: 10px;
            text-align: center;
        }

        th{
            background-color: lightblue;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<h2>Student Details</h2>

<table>
    <tr>
        <th>Roll No</th>
        <th>Name</th>
        <th>Course</th>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>101</td>
        <td>Anushka</td>
        <td>Computer Engineering</td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>102</td>
        <td>Rahul</td>
        <td>Information Technology</td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>103</td>
        <td>Priya</td>
        <td>Electronics</td>
    </tr>

</table>

</body>
</html>


Tag	Purpose
<table>	Creates a table
<tr>	Creates a table row
<th>	Creates a table heading
<td>	Creates a table data cell
rowspan	Merges rows
colspan	Merges columns
border	Adds a border (HTML attribute, though CSS is preferred)
